    about_en: ["Eli Magen and Adi Renert bring two worlds of song together: timeless classics of Hebrew song and the American standards on which jazz improvisation was built. The show rests on a simple idea: music has no borders, and Sasha Argov, Naomi Shemer and Shalom Hanoch can hold a conversation with Duke Ellington, Irving Berlin and George Gershwin.", "Out of these connections the two move between free, spontaneous playing and intimate performances in Magen’s deep voice."],
